KG42.register("clusters-ac244cd400fc0b1cb7be1a80",{"id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v142-d-K001","paper":"03-bilateral_p2p","label":"Bilateral price offers, contract selection, and price adjustment","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Bilateral price offers, contract selection, and price adjustment","market_meaning":"Taking potential trading relationships, current price offers, and actor preferences as inputs, each actor selects upstream and downstream contracts and adjusts price offers according to buyer selections and seller rejections until no prices change within a round. Real-time contract selection is additionally restricted by category-specific fulfillment conditions. This process takes a mutually agreed contract network as its candidate outcome, with stability remaining subject to the full substitutability assumption; the existing chains have not yet achieved complete closure of the mathematical and outcome interfaces.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","matching","activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The forward and real-time markets run the negotiation process separately, without merging price and contract states across the two stages. The shared R003 supports only fulfillment feasibility in real-time selection, with forward contracts serving here as existing commitments. The network structure in R004-C005 is limited to cases A/B, and R004-C006 retains only permission to extend the method; stable outcomes are conditional on full substitutability.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Price offers, contract selection, and conditional price adjustment jointly constitute the negotiation rule through explicit information feedback. R003's real-time feasibility conditions serve as shared support, while its independent fulfillment obligations have a separate primary assignment; participation permission lies outside this cluster. This boundary is proposed on the basis of the quantity and decision interfaces within the process.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retains the process description of buyers requesting discrete energy trades and progressively increasing price offers, read together with the conditional updates in R002, without counting an additional independent price-adjustment algorithm."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents price initialization, update-triggering conditions, the two price-adjustment branches, and the stopping criterion, constituting the price-state transition component of the negotiation process."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents potential trading relationships, contract selection in each round, and conditional network-outcome semantics, while retaining the distinction between case-study topology and the scope of the general method."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Serves only as support for fulfillment feasibility in real-time contract selection; its category-specific energy obligations are primarily assigned to v142-d-K002, and the shared reference is not counted as a second independent fulfillment rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-pb-omega","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"E19's account of buyers progressively increasing price offers is elaborated by the conditional buyer-price updates in E17. This connection retains the triggering conditions of the update branches and is not interpreted as requiring every buyer to increase its price in every round."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-pb-omega","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-ps-omega"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T007","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16"],"rationale":"In each round, buyer and seller prices are used to construct upstream and downstream candidate contract menus, respectively, which then enter actor selection. Only the quantity interface from prices to menus is established here, retaining R004's original role for the menus as local inputs."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Ystar-mi","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Zstar-mi","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Z-mi","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"Upstream and downstream selections in the same market and round, together with the portion of the menu not selected by sellers, provide inputs for the next conditional price adjustment. The mixed use of trade-set and contract-set types remains documented in G002; the candidate interface is retained here without supplying a projection for the original expression."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26"],"rationale":"E18 places the stopping criterion and the subsequently reported contract-network outcome within the same process, while R004 adds its market-outcome meaning and the full substitutability condition. This mapping links the semantic scopes of termination and outcome; it does not treat the stopping condition alone as a stability proof."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e36","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The conditions defining the finite-valued domains of real-time utility for the three actor categories restrict acceptable contract bundles, and E14 further explains that minimum contractual requirements are met before utility is improved. R003 therefore supports the feasibility of real-time selection, but this does not warrant a claim that C already contains complete utility functions or the physical execution process."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"The two chains reference the same frozen price-coordination node and both refer to this dual-market negotiation process. The representative is selected solely for display; the original node references and all their respective associated edges are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16"],"rationale":"The frozen nodes with the same name in the two chains both correspond to potential trading relationships and contract selection by both parties. Unified display does not amount to merging R002's conditional or ordering relationships with R004's original links edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Ystar-mi","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"Restricted to the same market, actor, and iteration, the two objects refer to the same set of selected upstream contracts. R002's operational role and R004's design_selection role are retained, without directly treating each round's selections as the final contracts to be fulfilled."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Zstar-mi","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"Restricted to the same market, actor, and iteration, the two objects refer to the same set of selected downstream contracts. The local roles as operational state and design selection are retained separately, and the trade/contract type uncertainty in the price-adjustment conditions is not removed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Z-mi","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T008"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"Both objects describe the downstream candidate menu constructed in the same round using current seller prices. The distinction between its role as an operational quantity in R002 and as a local input parameter in R004 remains unchanged; the menu is not interpreted as a quantity fixed across iterations."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All source quotations in this cluster remain unverified and are eligible only as experimental candidate support; no B source review, C2 independent review, or Agent E review was performed in this round.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e36","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E26"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the current evidence referenced by this cluster and the interpretations between chains item by item, paying particular attention to algorithmic symbols, conditions, and case-study scope; until then, retain their candidate character without changing source status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R002's update conditions directly treat trades as members of the selected-contract and rejected-contract sets, while R002 and R004 also declare these sets to be subsets of contracts carrying prices. The existing connections have not resolved the type difference between trades and contracts.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Ystar-mi","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Zstar-mi","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Z-mi","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p01","v141-b-g02-P1"],"required_work":"Check whether the original text uses an implicit trade-projection notation, and have upstream C clarify the type correspondence. D retains the original formulas and objects; the related contract-concept proposals remain pending."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing C does not represent, through complete constraints, menu reconstruction in each round, contract aggregation and the price vector after termination, or outcome feasibility requiring at most one contract per trade. R004's description of a stable network cannot replace these outcome interfaces.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T007","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p04","v141-b-g02-P2","v141-b-g02-P4","v141-b-g02-P5","v141-b-g03-P02-stable-contract-network"],"required_work":"Have upstream C add traceable menu-construction and final-outcome interfaces and clarify the applicability conditions for stability and equilibrium. Whether to adopt the related pending proposals is a separate manual decision; no graph objects or scientific expressions are added in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Full substitutability currently appears only as a textual premise in R004; C does not represent the complete utility functions or their testable conditions. In addition, there are discrepancies involving the two candidate transcriptions of Eq. (9) and the exponent notation in Eqs. (20)–(21). The appendix inequalities and parameter conditions still require mathematical review; the conclusion section cannot substitute for a stability argument.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T009","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-T010","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E01","v141-b-g03-E06-theorem1-forward-eq20-21","v141-b-g02-E26"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p03","v141-b-g02-P3","v141-b-g03-P01-full-substitutability"],"required_work":"Check the original notation and validity conditions of the risk-preference formulas and appendix proof, then have the upstream stage add the required preference constraints. At present, retain only the conditional stability result, without determining that all candidate preferences satisfy that condition."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The sets selected in each round in R004 and the forward and real-time contracts for fulfillment in R003 pertain to different stages and uses; they cannot be identified as the same quantity solely because their upstream and downstream symbols are similar. The existing C still lacks an explicit handoff from the final mutually agreed outcome to each actor's contracts for fulfillment.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-YFi","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-YRi","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-ZFi","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-ZRi","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e36","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p02"],"required_work":"Have the upstream stage clarify final acceptance, actor assignment, and the handoff of contract states from the forward to the real-time stage, retaining the established role of forward commitments in the real-time stage. No same_quantity mapping between these objects is established in this round."}]},"rule_refs":["03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R001","03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R002","03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R004","03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3a452a468ee069da","COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","COMP-844db09f135647e9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8"]});
